<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Root element is <Patch>, singular. <Patches> silently discards every
     operation in the file. -->
<Patch>

  <!-- Dubs Rimatomics ships two real benches and gives neither of them a room
       role, so the rooms they stand in score zero for every RoomRoleDef and
       come back as the generic "Room".

       That is the whole bug, and it is one field. RoomRoleWorker_Workshop and
       RoomRoleWorker_Laboratory score on exactly one thing —
       def.building.workTableRoomRole — and never look at the thingClass, even
       though TableRimatomicsMachining IS a Building_WorkTable and
       NuclearResearchBench IS a research bench. Vanilla sets the field on every
       one of its own benches; nothing makes a mod do the same.

       Verified in game 2026-09-13 with a control: two identical 9x9 rooms, a
       Rimatomics machining table in one and a vanilla TableMachining in the
       other. The vanilla room armed a stand for crafting, tailoring, smithing
       and art; the Rimatomics room reported "nothing; the game reads this room
       as: Room".

       NO SPEED PENALTY COMES WITH THIS. The "not in optimal room" malus is a
       SEPARATE field, workTableNotInRoomRoleFactor, which defaults to 1f, and
       StatPart_WorkTableRoomRole bails out at 1f
       (StatPart_WorkTableRoomRole.cs:41). Setting only the role is inert for
       gameplay: it changes room scoring and adds an "optimal room" line to the
       info card, nothing else. We deliberately do not set the factor —
       inventing a work-speed penalty for somebody else's bench is not a
       compatibility fix.

       The reactor hall is NOT fixable here and is not attempted: it holds no
       work table at all, so there is no def to hang the field on. That case is
       handled in the assembly, by contents — see RoomContentsWork.

       Everything is guarded by mod NAME (PatchOperationFindMod matches display
       names, not packageIds), then per-def existence, then per-field existence.
       So the file is a silent no-op without the mod, survives a def rename with
       nothing worse than that def staying vanilla, and stands down entirely if
       Rimatomics ever sets the field itself.

       The ensure-then-append shape on <building> is not ceremony. Two mods that
       each Add a container node to the same def do not merge: the loader
       reports "defines the same field twice" and keeps only the last one, so a
       bare Add of <building> here would delete whatever another Rimatomics
       patch had put in that node, depending on load order. Test for the
       container, create it only when absent, then add the field into it. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Dubs Rimatomics</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- The nuclear machining table is a Building_WorkTable; its bills are
             Smithing work (DoBillsTableNuclear), which a Workshop stand already
             covers. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="TableRimatomicsMachining"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
                <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="TableRimatomicsMachining"]/building</xpath>
                <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                  <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="TableRimatomicsMachining"]</xpath>
                  <value>
                    <building />
                  </value>
                </nomatch>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
                <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="TableRimatomicsMachining"]/building/workTableRoomRole</xpath>
                <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                  <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="TableRimatomicsMachining"]/building</xpath>
                  <value>
                    <workTableRoomRole>Workshop</workTableRoomRole>
                  </value>
                </nomatch>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!-- The Rimatomics research bench. Laboratory already resolves to
             Research AND Crafting, and their research giver exists under both
             work types (RimatomicsResearch, RimatomicsCrafting), so the role is
             all that was missing. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="NuclearResearchBench"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
                <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="NuclearResearchBench"]/building</xpath>
                <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                  <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="NuclearResearchBench"]</xpath>
                  <value>
                    <building />
                  </value>
                </nomatch>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
                <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="NuclearResearchBench"]/building/workTableRoomRole</xpath>
                <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                  <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="NuclearResearchBench"]/building</xpath>
                  <value>
                    <workTableRoomRole>Laboratory</workTableRoomRole>
                  </value>
                </nomatch>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
